  "comedy": {
    "hook": "A tiny mosquito sits on the cheek of a man who thinks one slap will solve it.",
    "goal": "Hit the mosquito.",
    "escalation": [
      "The first slap hits only his own cheek.",
      "Changing hands produces the same painful result.",
      "Using both hands only squashes his own face."
    ],
    "payoff": "He folds his hands in surrender while the mosquito sits on his head.",
    "callback": "The tiny unhurt opponent returns while the man has two red cheeks."
  },
  "title": "Machhar Bacha, Thappad Khud Ko",
  "story": "A mosquito sits on a man’s right cheek. He smiles, aims carefully and slaps, but the mosquito flies away first. His own slap squashes his face. It lands on his other cheek; the same thing happens with the other hand. Angry now, he prepares to squash it between both palms on his nose. It escapes again, and his face squashes between his own hands. He opens his empty hands, then folds them in surrender. The mosquito calmly sits on his head while he gives the viewer a defeated stare.",
